# Git pathspecs for everything a release's packages are built from: the inputs
# to the binary plus every file nfpm.yaml and nfpm-gtk.yaml package. Test files
# are compiled into nothing.
#
# A commit that touches none of these changes nothing a user installs. It does
# not trigger the automatic release, and generate-changelog.sh leaves it out of
# the changelog, so a CI tool bump never reads as a change to the package.
#
# Keep this in step with nfpm.yaml and nfpm-gtk.yaml. A packaged file missing
# from here is not lost: a change to it simply waits for the next release, and
# that release's changelog does not mention it.
#
# One pathspec per line. Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.

cmd
internal
go.mod
go.sum
nfpm.yaml
systemd
config
packaging
LICENSE
README.md
docs/retrosaver.1
scripts/postinstall.sh
nfpm-gtk.yaml
gui
docs/retrosaver-settings.1
:(exclude)*_test.go
:(exclude)gui/test_*.py
